  "id": "hpa",
  "term": "HPA",
  "definition": "HPA stands for the hypothalamic–pituitary–adrenal axis, a major neuroendocrine system that helps regulate the body’s stress response. In the source, disrupted HPA activity after stroke is described as contributing to prolonged stress-hormone imbalance and to later emotional and cognitive problems such as depression, anxiety, and cognitive impairment.",
